35,2,1,talk,Shion,,"It's exactly as I suspected. The wall is practically transparent to sound, and our desks are becoming dining tables. We are dealing with both a privacy leak and a hygiene problem.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found out that we spent 68,000 yen on outside rentals last year for very small groups. Also, the meeting fit-out is 141,000 yen, while the kitchen is 96,000. It's... a lot of money.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,I found out that only two people use the room almost all the time! And the old fridge was a disaster—half the stuff was abandoned and one person had to clean it up over and over!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It seems we are lacking a sanctuary for the heart. Our spontaneous conversations have dwindled to the printer, and our most difficult moments are played out in public, leaving scars of silence. We need a place for genuine connection.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The facilities data shows that simple rooms with only chairs cause no trouble. However, the time spent walking for lunch is significant—twenty-five minutes a trip. We are losing a great deal of time to basic needs.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Daisuke, the outside hire costs prove we need a dedicated meeting space, but @Servas is right about the privacy. If the wall is this thin, a ""Meeting Space"" needs to be handled carefully, or we'll just be eavesdropping.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I see. If we keep paying for outside rooms, we're just spending money every month. But 141,000 yen for a meeting room is a big one-time cost. I'm worried about who has to sign for that.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"But if we make it a kitchen, will it just get gross again? I saw that one person did all the cleaning! That's not fair. We should pick something that everyone helps with, not just one person!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Servas,,"Rin, your heart is in the right place. Fairness is the foundation of any shared space. If we create a room for connection, we must ensure it is a burden to none and a blessing to all.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shion, if we prioritize a meeting space, we must consider the maintenance. @Rin, your point about the fridge is valid; a kitchen creates a recurring labor burden that often falls on a single person. We must avoid that.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shion,,"If we want to stop the crumbs at our desks and the waste of time Toshio mentioned, a kitchen is logical. But Rin's point about the cleaning burden is a real risk. Perhaps a Quiet Room is the most efficient?","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I don't know. A Quiet Room might be cheaper, but it doesn't solve the outside hire costs. If we keep renting rooms, we're just spending money that could have paid for the fit-out.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I don't want a Quiet Room! That sounds boring. We need a place where we can actually do things together, but we have to promise to clean up our own messes this time!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Servas,,"A place for silence has its merits, but we are starving for connection. If we only seek efficiency, we forget the human spirit. We need a space where we can speak honestly and grow closer.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, connection is valuable, but not at the cost of efficiency or unfair labor. A kitchen solves the lunch commute and desk mess, yet risks the cleaning cycle Rin fears. A meeting space addresses the rental costs.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shion,,"Let's be realistic. A Quiet Room solves nothing. A kitchen solves the mess and the commute but creates a cleaning nightmare. A Meeting Space stops the rental drain and provides the privacy Servas wants, provided we manage the noise.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think a Meeting Space makes the most sense for the budget. If we stop the outside rentals, the fit-out pays for itself eventually. I just hope we can agree on how to manage it.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I still think a kitchen would be fun, but if everyone says the cleaning is too hard, then a Meeting Space is okay! As long as we all use it and not just two people!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Servas,,"If we choose a Meeting Space, let us ensure it is not merely for business, but a sanctuary for the difficult and the honest conversations that our spirits currently lack. I support this path.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,The logic is sound. A Meeting Space eliminates the rental drain and avoids the recurring maintenance burden of a kitchen. It is the most sustainable choice for our time and labor. I agree.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
